id: pm-2tan
title: "Plan positional-action help is undiscoverable: pm plan create --help is rejected as an unknown command"
description: Make the documented plan action grammar self-describing so agents can inspect exact create and step flags without falling into generic unknown-command recovery.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli",contracts,help,plan
created_at: "2026-07-15T20:00:17.934Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-18T11:14:26.459Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-18T11:12:20.200Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-18T11:12:20.200Z"
author: codex-audit-20260715
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "pm plan create --help and --help --json resolve to action-specific help or an equally precise positional-action help view; pm help plan create and command-scoped contracts expose the same effective flags; shell completion advertises plan actions; pm plan --help no longer reports an empty subcommands array while describing subcommands only in a positional argument; documented pm plan create examples remain valid; regression tests cover help JSON, contracts, completion, and unknown-command recovery"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: All positional plan/assurance actions and standard commands expose consistent full-path structured help; compact contracts retain action discovery while targeted/full projections restore exact format budgets.
expected_result: "Agents can inspect every positional plan/assurance action before execution through direct help, generic help, completion, or command contracts without an unknown-command detour."
actual_result: "Bounded default contracts retain all 27 action paths while omitting repeated detail; command-scoped/full output restores it, standard help includes resolved paths, and the search-active discovery ratchet now measures all 27 virtual action help paths across 99 surfaces."
