  "2026-07-15T20:00:17.934Z",codex-audit-20260715,"Duplicate check evidence: all-status searches for plan create help unknown command positional action contracts found only broad roadmap and historical audit entries with no focused active or terminal owner."
  "2026-08-04T09:18:06.510Z","harness:codex","Fresh agent-recovery evidence 2026-08-04: following the apparent plan-link contract as pm plan link <plan> --link <item> produced a recovery error requiring an undocumented positional step reference. The generic plan help reports usage [subcommand] [id] [stepRef] but its sole example is pm init, so it does not demonstrate link syntax. After discovering the hidden positional requirement, pm plan link pm-gzyt2j plan-step-002 --link ... succeeded. This remains a live avoidable agent stall."
  "2026-08-04T09:34:37.917Z","harness:codex","Fresh contract/runtime parity evidence 2026-08-04: pm contracts --command update --flags-only --json advertises extension-provided --allow-audit-update and --allow-audit-dep-update as supported update flags, but invoking pm update pm-gzyt2j ... --allow-audit-update is rejected by Commander as Unknown option. Retrying the same update without the advertised flag succeeds. Action-specific help/contracts must describe the actually registered command path, including extension-injected flags, or agents cannot trust the prescribed runtime contract discovery workflow."
  "2026-08-16T19:24:32.738Z","harness:codex","Fresh recurrence evidence 2026-08-16: the newly added, fully executable `pm assurance risk --definition <json> --json` action succeeds through the direct CLI, SDK transport, and packed npx/bunx installation, but `pm assurance risk --help --json` exits 2 with unknown_command. Generic `pm assurance --help --json` exposes an empty subcommands array, labels --definition only as Put declaration JSON, and redirects action discovery to contracts. This is the same positional-action help defect already owned here; no duplicate item was created."
  "2026-08-18T04:51:56.149Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-18: one coupled SDK/CLI/MCP tranche will make positional actions and recovery references contract-declared, executable, parity-gated, and discoverable. Scope includes generated contracts, public SDK types, CLI help and recovery, MCP aliases, assurance negative controls, documentation, temporary-workspace acceptance, and packed npm/Bun consumers. Duplicate check used the complete 2,521-item all-status corpus with zero omissions or truncation."
  "2026-08-18T06:29:31.138Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: full literal all-source coverage passed 519 files and 7,540 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 after compatibility checks preserved the richer plan/schema/profile missing-subcommand recovery. Compact contracts retain parent command summaries while full contracts add all 27 plan/assurance action summaries."
  "2026-08-18T06:45:40.614Z","harness:codex","Closeout evidence: positional plan and assurance action help now resolves through both direct and generic help paths; parent JSON help lists actions; full contracts expose all 27 action summaries/signatures while compact output stays bounded; completion derives from the same contract. PM-linked focused execution passed 8/8 tests, aggregate literal coverage passed 7,540 tests at exact 100/100/100/100, and packed npm/npx/bunx acceptance passed."
  "2026-08-18T08:04:18.993Z","harness:codex","Independent review start: compact command summaries must retain all positional action paths, with focused multi-token action and availability/schema projections."
